  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request Details**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. It\'s clear they want visually appealing, interactive icons for their websites. The challenge lies in translating \"bonitos\" into specific aesthetic qualities, and in understanding the level of interactivity desired. I\'m focusing on defining \"interactive\" in this context and brainstorming potential visual styles that align with both terms.\n\n\n**Defining the Studio Concept**\n\nI\'m now solidifying the core concept. It\'s becoming clearer: an \"Interactive Icon Studio\" is the aim, encompassing creation, customization, and export for website icons. I envision a curated library categorized by function (Navigation, Media, etc.) with various interactive behaviors like hover animations (bounce, spin, morph) and click animations (burst, toggle, ripple). There are many design themes to explore, starting with Modern Glassmorphism.\n\n\n**Exploring Icon Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve been exploring a range of aesthetics. I\'m imagining duotone neon glow, minimalist monochrome, soft claymorphism, and even retro pixel styles. The goal is to provide a diverse selection. I\'m also now considering a custom color picker, with options for primary and secondary colors, glow, stroke width, and corner roundness. There are frame and background badge options, too.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
