  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Interactive Icons**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the architecture for AuraIcons. The user wants interactive, beautiful icons for their websites. I\'m currently pondering the specific qualities that make an icon \"interactive and very pretty\" in a web context. I need to define these qualities and design an architecture to facilitate their creation.\n\n\n**Cataloging Icon Variations**\n\nI\'ve been creating an extensive catalog. I\'m imagining a rich collection of handcrafted, morphing icons. The catalog includes diverse icon types: navigation, user & social, commerce & business, media & audio, interface & system, and tech & AI. I\'m focusing on descriptive verbs and actions for each to emphasize interactivity, from a menu morphing to a close button to a shopping cart rolling with an item drop.\n\n\n**Defining Interactive Properties**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into interactive behaviors. I\'m imagining how specific hover states could work, with examples like a hamburger menu morphing into an \"X,\" or a play button morphing into a pause icon. I\'m focusing on \"spring\" effects, pulsing glows, stroke drawing, and 3D tilts. I am also exploring click/tap feedback, including optional haptic or audio cues.\n\n\n**Enumerating Customization Options**\n\nI\'m now outlining a robust customization engine. I\'m focusing on aesthetic styles, like glassmorphic aura and cyber neon, and linear minimal for Apple. Custom color pickers will be key. I\'m exploring dimensions and controls, including stroke width, sizes, and animation speed for a range of interaction triggers.\n\n\n**Outlining Deployment Methods**\n\nI am now focusing on providing a spectrum of deployment options to users. I plan to support raw SVG with inline CSS for broad compatibility. I\'ll also offer downloadable SVG files and snippets for Vue and HTML. Further, I want users to preview the icons in realistic web UI components: a navbar, feature card, FAB, CTA button, and a reaction bar. I am imagining all the ways people may want to see and use the icons.\n\n\n**Structuring the Codebase**\n\nI\'m now focused on organizing the codebase for AuraIcons, to create a smooth user experience. I\'ve designed a clear directory structure: `src/types/icon.ts` will contain all the necessary definitions; `src/data/iconsList.ts` will house the icon library; `src/utils/audio.ts` will implement Web Audio API for feedback; and `src/utils/codeGenerators.ts` generates different code outputs. The rendering logic lives in `InteractiveIcon.tsx`, the design space is `IconStudioCanvas.tsx`, and the show case is `WebContextsShowcase.tsx`. I need instant 1-click copy functionality.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5379393"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false,\"CodeContent\":\"export type IconCategory =\\n  | \'all\'\\n  | \'navigation\'\\n  | \'actions\'\\n  | \'commerce\'\\n  | \'media\'\\n  | \'interface\'\\n  | \'social\'\\n  | \'tech\';\\n\\nexport type IconStyleTheme =\\n  | \'glass\'\\n  | \'neon\'\\n  | \'minimal\'\\n  | \'sunset\'\\n  | \'duotone\'\\n  | \'cyber\'\\n  | \'emerald\';\\n\\nexport type AnimationType =\\n  | \'bounce\'\\n  | \'morph\'\\n  | \'pulse\'\\n  | \'glow\'\\n  | \'spin\'\\n  | \'tilt\'\\n  | \'shake\'\\n  | \'strokeDraw\'\\n  | \'burst\'\\n  | \'heartbeat\';\\n\\nexport type TriggerMode = \'hover\' | \'click\' | \'loop\' | \'magnetic\';\\n\\nexport interface InteractiveIconDef {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  nameEs: string;\\n  category: IconCategory;\\n  tags: string[];\\n  description: string;\\n  defaultAnimation: AnimationType;\\n  // Morph alternate icon or state if applicable\\n  morphTarget?: string;\\n  badge?: string | number;\\n  // Specific SVG paths or instructions\\n  paths: {\\n    d: string;\\n    strokeWidth?: number;\\n    fill?: string;\\n    stroke?: string;\\n    strokeLinecap?: \'round\' | \'inherit\' | \'butt\' | \'square\';\\n    strokeLinejoin?: \'round\' | \'inherit\' | \'miter\' | \'bevel\';\\n    className?: string;\\n    style?: React.CSSProperties;\\n    animatedProps?: Record<string, unknown>;\\n  }[];\\n  customRender?: (props: IconRenderProps) => React.ReactNode;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface IconRenderProps {\\n  size: number;\\n  strokeWidth: number;\\n  primaryColor: string;\\n  secondaryColor: string;\\n  accentColor: string;\\n  isHovered: boolean;\\n  isActive: boolean;\\n  isToggled: boolean;\\n  theme: IconStyleTheme;\\n  animation: AnimationType;\\n  triggerMode: TriggerMode;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface StudioSettings {\\n  searchQuery: string;\\n  selectedCategory: IconCategory;\\n  selectedTheme: IconStyleTheme;\\n  strokeWidth: number;\\n  iconSize: number;\\n  primaryColor: string;\\n  secondaryColor: string;\\n  accentColor: string;\\n  animationSpeed: number; // 0.5 (fast) to 2 (slow)\\n  triggerMode: TriggerMode;\\n  enableMagnetic: boolean;\\n  enableSound: boolean;\\n  enableParticles: boolean;\\n  containerShape: \'none\' | \'squircle\' | \'circle\' | \'square\' | \'glass\';\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create type definitions for interactive icon studio\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/icon.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating icon types\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create src/types/icon.ts\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
